Data Loading & Preprocessing

    Loads the airports data from a CSV file.
    Renames columns to standardized names.
    Uses TimezoneFinder (with pytz) to fill in missing timezone information.
    Drops rows with missing values.

Distance & Flight Time Calculations

    Computes Euclidean (straight-line) distances from JFK to each airport.
    Computes geodesic (Haversine) distances from JFK to each airport.
    Estimates flight times based on an average speed (900 km/h).
    Uses KMeans clustering to group airports based on their geographic coordinates.

Database Query Functions

    Distance Verification: Retrieves sample flight distances from the flights table to compare with computed distances.

    NYC Departure Airports: Identifies airports (from the airports table) that serve as origins for NYC flights.

    Flight Destinations on a Given Day: Retrieves and visualizes the destinations for flights departing from a specified airport on a specific month and day.

    Flight Statistics for a Given Day: Retrieves flight destinations along with basic statistics for a given day from a specified airport.
    
    Plane Types on Route: Determines the types of planes used on a specified route (by counting tail numbers and mapping them to plane types).
    
    Average Departure Delay per Airline: Calculates average departure delays for each airline and merges the results with airline names for visualization.
    
    Delayed Flights for Destination: Counts the number of delayed flights (based on arrival delay) for a given destination within a specified range of months.
    
    Top Airplane Manufacturers for Destination: Identifies the top five airplane manufacturers for flights arriving at a specified destination.
    
    Relationship Between Distance and Arrival Delay: Plots a scatter plot of flight distances versus arrival delays and computes the correlation between the two.
    
    Average Speed per Plane: Computes the average speed for each plane (using distance and air time) and updates the planes table with this value.
    
    Flight Direction Calculation: Computes the bearing (direction) from NYC (JFK) to each airport.
    
    Inner Product of Flight Direction and Wind:
        Calculates the bearing from NYC to the destination airport.
        Retrieves weather data (wind speed and direction) for the flight's origin and date.
        Computes the inner product between the flight direction vector and the wind vector.
    
    Relationship Between Wind Direction and Air Time:
        Iterates through a sample of flights.
        Computes the inner product for each flight and categorizes it by sign (positive/negative).
        Visualizes the relationship between the inner product sign and the air time using a box plot.

Visualization Functions

    Scatter Plots:
        World airports scatter map.
        US airports scatter map.
        Scatter plots for altitude versus estimated flight time and geodesic distance versus altitude.
        Scatter_geo heatmaps for geodesic and Euclidean distances.
        Map of airports colored by time zone.

    Bar Charts & Histograms:
        Bar chart for the distribution of airports by time zone.
        Histograms for Euclidean distance, geodesic distance, and estimated flight time.

    Pie Charts:
        Pie charts for the distribution of airports by time zone.

    Route Plotting:
        Visualizes flight routes from JFK to a list of specified destination airports using color-coded lines (based on geodesic distance).

Main Function

    Ties together data loading, calculations, visualizations, and database queries.
    Prompts the user for input (FAA codes) to plot flight routes.
    Executes all functions sequentially to produce a comprehensive dashboard/analysis upon running the script.